  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/d8f735790daf267a094ecd8c336d90de65d84e3985485213eb541364bd14aacd.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ we get only the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t,\\,t\\in (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].\n$$",
